  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nA ~1035 mb area of high pressure positioned over the region \nearly this morning will shift southward to the mid Atlantic \ncoast by later today. Subsidence from the high will provide \ncontinued dry conditions, sunny skies, light winds and \nseasonable conditions today. Tonight will be seasonable chilly \nagain with lows in the upper 20s to mid 30s. On Mon, a cold \nfront approaching from SE Canada will push southeast across the \narea during the afternoon to early evening hours. Just a few \nlight showers may occur in the W. Adirondacks, otherwise the \nfront will pass through dry. Temperatures should be able to warm\ninto the mid 60s in many valley areas ahead of the front. Winds\nwill shift to the northwest late in the day, with gusts of \n15-20 mph developing in spots. A colder air mass will filter in \nMon night through the middle of the week, with below normal \ntemperatures expected. It will be dry though, as another area of\nhigh pressure builds in. As the high shifts south/east on Thu, \na milder S/SW flow will results in warmer temperatures. Another \nmoisture-starved cold front is expected to pass through on Fri, \nalthough temperatures don't look as cold behind this front.",
